Feature: Create and populate the sample_sales_data table in Unity Catalog

  Background:
    Given the Unity Catalog schema "purgo_playground" exists

  Scenario: Successfully create the sample_sales_data table
    When the "sample_sales_data" table is created with columns "country_cd" (string), "product_id" (string), "qty_sold" (int), and "sales_date" (date)
    Then the table "purgo_playground.sample_sales_data" should exist with the correct schema

  Scenario Outline: Successfully insert data into the sample_sales_data table
    Given the table "purgo_playground.sample_sales_data" exists
    When the following data is inserted into the table:
      | country_cd | product_id | qty_sold | sales_date |
      | <country> | <product> | <qty>    | <date>    |
    Then the data should exist in the table "purgo_playground.sample_sales_data"

    Examples:
      | country | product | qty | date       |
      | US      | P1001  | 50  | 2024-01-15 |
      | US      | P1002  | 30  | 2024-01-16 |
      | CA      | P1001  | 40  | 2024-01-15 |
      | CA      | P1003  | 25  | 2024-01-17 |
      | UK      | P1002  | 35  | 2024-01-18 |
      | UK      | P1004  | 20  | 2024-01-19 |
      | IN      | P1001  | 60  | 2024-01-20 |
      | IN      | P1003  | 45  | 2024-01-21 |
      | AU      | P1004  | 55  | 2024-01-22 |
      | AU      | P1002  | 38  | 2024-01-23 |


  Scenario Outline: Attempt to insert data with invalid data type
    Given the table "purgo_playground.sample_sales_data" exists
    When the following data is inserted into the table:
      | country_cd | product_id | qty_sold | sales_date |
      | <country> | <product> | <qty>    | <date>    |
    Then the insertion should fail with error message "<error_message>"

    Examples:
      | country | product | qty    | date      | error_message                                     |
      | US      | P1001  | "fifty" | 2024-01-15 | Invalid data type for qty_sold: expected int      |
      | US      | P1002  | 30     | "invalid" | Invalid data type for sales_date: expected date |

  Scenario: Attempt to insert data with null values for non-nullable columns
    Given the table "purgo_playground.sample_sales_data" exists
    When the following data is inserted into the table:
      | country_cd | product_id | qty_sold | sales_date |
      | ""         | P1001      | 50       | 2024-01-15 |
    Then the insertion should fail with error message "country_cd cannot be null"

  Scenario: Attempt to insert data with duplicate primary key (if defined)
    Given the table "purgo_playground.sample_sales_data" exists and has a primary key defined
    And the following data already exists in the table:
      | country_cd | product_id | qty_sold | sales_date |
      | US         | P1001      | 50       | 2024-01-15 |
    When the following data is inserted into the table:
      | country_cd | product_id | qty_sold | sales_date |
      | US         | P1001      | 60       | 2024-01-15 |
    Then the insertion should fail with error message "Duplicate primary key violation"